Description: Use libtool 2.4.6's FreeBSD library versioning
 libao 1.2.0 ships the ltmain.sh of GNU libtool 2.4.2, which names a FreeBSD
 shared library after libtool's "current" interface number alone: libao's
 -version-info 5:0:1 gives libao.so.5. Later GNU libtool (2.4.6, the version in
 gmp 6.3.0's tarball) versions freebsd-elf as current - age, as on Linux,
 which gives upstream's soname libao.so.4 (also FreeBSD's). This is that hunk
 of libtool 2.4.6's ltmain.sh, copied unchanged.
Origin: GNU libtool 2.4.6, build-aux/ltmain.sh (freebsd-elf case of the
 version_type switch)
Forwarded: not-needed (fixed in later libtool; libao has had no release since
 1.2.0)
---
--- a/ltmain.sh
+++ b/ltmain.sh
@@ -7414,8 +7414,9 @@
 	  ;;
 
 	freebsd-elf)
-	  major=".$current"
-	  versuffix=".$current"
+	  func_arith $current - $age
+	  major=.$func_arith_result
+	  versuffix=$major.$age.$revision
 	  ;;
 
 	irix | nonstopux)
